WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:06.529
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, thanks for submitting
questions for this week’s doctor who Q&amp;A.

00:00:06.529 --> 00:00:08.670
And thanks to everyone who’s commented on
the new look I have going on here.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.700
I am working on sound proofing so there won’t
be an echo anymore.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.050
I just flipped my camera around so it wasn’t
the white wall.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.049
I just thought this would be more fun to stare
at.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:22.660
Here are a few quick additional notes from
the episode before we get to questions.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.300
First commenter Jon Ellis pointed out that
The Cave where the merry men hid out was also

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.950
the place they filmed the Sherlock hound of
baskerville episode.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:40.230
And the doctor has been seen with matt smith’s
sonic filming in future episodes.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:46.210
So he didn’t permanently lose it.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.109
I address the deleted scene in the q&amp;a.

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:53.890
But careful for spoilers from robot of sherwood
if you haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.649
I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:56.719
Here we go

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:00.190
Question 1 - Kevin G asks Is the Promised
Land Gallifrey?

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:04.770
I definitely think Gallifrey, The Promised
Land and Missy’s Heaven are all connected.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.740
Even if they’re not all the same place.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.180
We know Gallifrey is in the pocket Universe
and we know Missy is the Gatekeeper of the

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.210
Nethersphere.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.950
We don’t know what that is yet, but because
of all the dead people she’s saving it’s

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.960
implied that she might have time lord like
abilities.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.430
After Deep Breath initially I thought the
promised land was more of a metaphor unique

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.960
to each character.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.950
Like the clockwork droid’s idea of the promised
land was something created by his own mind.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.020
And the Doctor’s idea of the promised land
was gallifrey.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:37.320
I don’t think the robots in episode 3 or
the clockwork droids were trying to get to

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.320
Gallifrey.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.930
Otherwise the screen would have read gallifrey.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:47.399
I think they’re responding to a summons
of sorts.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:52.360
Like something is calling them to the promised
land.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.360
That could be missy’s doing.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.950
But it starting to seem like everyone will
have the same reason for wanting to go there.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:04.060
Question 2 - Hydra da Little asks Earth has
a twin planet called Mondas, what if that’s

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.070
what the Promised Land image was?

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:12.409
Another good theory, Cybermen play a big role
this series in some mysterious way.

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:15.730
If gallifrey is coming back, so could mondas
too.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.460
There have been a lot of spoilery images of
the finale that add some fuel to the fire

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.280
but since a lot of you requested I not show
them.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.680
I’ll let you guys just do a google image
search.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.610
In terms of specific planets there are a few
strong candidates that I’ll mention in a

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.610
slightly different question later in this
video.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.269
I’m also starting to think of the promised
land as a missy trap of sorts.

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:35.670
Maybe not a trap for the doctor, but a trap
for everyone else.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.880
It would sync up with the idea of robin hood
entering the archery contest knowing full

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:49.370
well it was a trap.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:58.960
Question 3 - Big ‘N Wide asks there have
been reports of a lot of familiar filming

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.370
locations from the place Kamelion was killed
by the fifth doctor as well as Fires of Pompeii

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.569
imagery.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:09.409
All tying in with the idea the doctor is leaving
himself subconscious messages.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:13.569
What are some theories for how this will be
explained?

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:16.099
Right now from a third person perspective
it seems like the common theme of the reminders

00:03:16.099 --> 00:03:18.330
is that The Doctor has been playing god.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.360
Altering time when it suits him, choosing
who he saves and who he allows to die.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.040
Usually you leave yourself a reminder when
you want to remember to take an action.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:41.040
I’m hoping the next villain Ms Delphox and
the futuristic bank gives us some more clues.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:47.420
That episode is number 5, so it’s in 2 weeks.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:53.030
Question 4 - Matt dosko asks Which historical
character do you want the doctor to meet next?

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.900
I’m really looking forward to the Mummy
on the Orient express episode and who might

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.900
show up in that from egyptian mythology.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.610
I don’t know who Foxes is playing, but I
think it’s just a lounge singer, I don’t

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.860
think she’s playing cleopatra.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:08.640
Question 5 - Oli Kidsley asks Do you like
the faster pace of the episodes so far?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.500
This episode felt like it was meant to be
more of a reflection on the journey so far.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.980
Yes, I do really like Capaldi’s pacing.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:25.830
I think a lot of it has to do with what the
actor’s bring to the role.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.900
Capaldi developed this amazing persona with
Malcolm Tucker.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:33.479
So I think it’s much more natural for him
as an actor to replicate that energy.

00:04:33.479 --> 00:04:37.380
But it’s fun to see him change that and
hold back in a scene.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.940
Like with the apple and the sonic.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.730
It makes watching the really old classic who
episodes a trip, just because television in

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:48.780
general was much more about long dialogue
scenes.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:56.050
And now you see a lot more jump cutting and
explosions.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:00.770
Question 6 - Joey Gmaj asks how do you feel
about the BBC cutting the beheading scene?

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.590
Did you want to see it?

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.380
I think it was totally appropriate given real
life circumstances.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.270
Their reason for taking it out was good.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:10.630
I didn’t watch the leaked episodes so I
didn’t know what the scene was.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:18.090
I’ve read since then that it presents the
Sheriff as a half man half robot.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:21.660
Mark Gatiss said technically he didn’t write
Robot of Sherwood to fit inside the Missy

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:26.210
plot, but it’s possible that the half man
half robot thing was foreshadowing for cybermen?

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.250
I’m okay without seeing it though.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.900
I don’t think it’s a huge deal.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.300
If it were something really really big, they’d
probably just post it digitally so people

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.490
could watch it if they wanted.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:39.949
Question 7 - The New View Production says,
Rachel Talalay the director of the finale

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:43.630
said to count the number of planets in the
opening titles.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:47.140
Is there a hint about missy in this?

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:52.919
Yes, here’s the message she tweeted out
that you’re referring to.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.240
She posted this very recently.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.350
And for reference, she directed both the final
two episodes.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.849
it’s a two parter, but they’re airing
them one week apart.

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:02.110
They won’t air back to back.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:06.050
Most of what I’ve read about this focuses
more on the big big planet that we can see

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.139
really well.

00:06:09.139 --> 00:06:14.340
The best theories are that this is gallifrey
or it’s a post-war trenzalore.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:17.740
The other planets could be moons and Gallifrey
does have or did have two moons.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.680
Supposedly they were destroyed during the
time war.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.700
But because of the 50th those could be back
with gallifrey.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.280
After staring at this and thinking more about
trenzalore I had the thought that it might

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.240
be more evidence capaldi is the actual fulfillment
of the silence’s prophecy about the first

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.330
question.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:34.330
Capaldi has made a very big deal about “Questions”
so far.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.620
Just more things to add to the theory pile.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.560
But just as a reminder going forward, as we
get more information about Missy and the promised

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.560
land.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:46.509
Think about the planets in the title sequence
and how they all might be connected.

00:06:46.509 --> 00:06:51.430
Question 8 - Michelle Sloney asks this episode
reminded me of the classic who episode where

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.790
the doctor met all the fairy tale characters.

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.400
Which episode was that?

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.430
You’re thinking of the Mind Robber from
the second doctor’s run.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:02.170
I don’t know if Mark Gatiss wrote it this
way intentionally but the story of that episode

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.910
had some similar themes.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:09.850
The fairy tale characters call the Doctor
a traitor because they view him as a fairy

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.280
tale character who rebelled.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.629
Robin Hood’s speech at the end of this week’s
episode was all about the thought that it

00:07:15.629 --> 00:07:19.360
doesn’t matter whether or not the story
is real, just that the story serves as a call

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.250
to action for people reading it.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:25.360
It’s a nice meta-commentary on the power
of fiction.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:30.130
Part of me wants to think that Missy is someone
inspired by The Doctor’s story and is doing

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.930
what she believes to be a great work in his
name.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.830
Like saving people for him.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:39.509
Like she’s his crazy fan.

00:07:39.509 --> 00:07:44.789
Question 9 - Paul Cagliarini asks what do
you think of the Madame de Pompadour Missy

00:07:44.789 --> 00:07:45.789
theory.

00:07:45.789 --> 00:07:49.379
The robots were a more advanced version of
the clockwork droids, so it’s possible Missy

00:07:49.379 --> 00:07:50.919
has Madame de Pompadour’s brain?

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:54.419
That’s definitely an interesting way to
think about her.

00:07:54.419 --> 00:07:58.190
Madame de Pompadour could still be holding
on to her idea of the doctor as her boyfriend

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:02.520
if her brain has survived in a very advanced
robot body.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.550
And as cool as the thought is, I’m really
hoping Missy turns out to be a completely

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:08.550
new character.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:13.449
I have a feeling that if she is an old classic
who character, no matter what the explanation

00:08:13.449 --> 00:08:16.000
is, most people will wind up dissapointed.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.720
Fan theories like the ones we talk about here
are always going to be way more complicated

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.120
and interesting that the reality.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.120
I think Missy being someone new or new as
in, she’s someone from the doctor’s past,

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.919
but not someone the show has done before.

00:08:27.919 --> 00:08:31.750
I think that just gives Moffat and future
showrunners more material to work with.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:35.410
I just feel like people would get tired of
it faster if they just kept recycling old

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:40.690
things over and over.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:46.010
Question 10 - Trent McIntire asks do you think
when Moffat leaves we’ll see the master

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:47.010
again?

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:53.250
I took this more as a do you think future
showrunners will bring other old stuff back.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:57.050
There’s definitely things Moffat has said
he’s not touching because Russell Davies

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.050
did them.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:02.000
Or things he didn’t want to do because he
thought he had nothing worthwhile to add.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.960
I think of all the things he hasn’t done,
future showrunners would probably search for

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:09.410
the most open ended stories from classic who
to build on.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:14.580
Like ones that focused more on characters
that already haven’t been done again in

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:15.690
new Who.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.000
Since Davies did the Master, I’m betting
unless Missy is a female master, we won’t

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.220
see him again until the next anniversary special.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:36.750
The 10th anniversary of New Who is March 26th
2015.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:41.530
Since the christmas special is the next big
special, I don’t know that the BBC is producing

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.480
any special content.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.030
But hopefully by the series 8 finale.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:54.560
They’ll let us know whether or not a 10th
anniversary episode is coming.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.280
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.580
These are always a ton of fun.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.940
I’m really liking series 8 so far.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.140
There’s so many new things to theorycraft.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.610
My next bonus video will be for my favorite
scary doctor who stories just because Listen

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:11.210
looks like it’s going to be pretty scary.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.271
Be sure to subscribe to get that.

00:10:12.271 --> 00:10:13.271
I’ll try to post it before episode 4 airs.

00:10:13.271 --> 00:10:15.370
